        "message": "I am deeply disappointed and concerned about the use of an image of an Israeli soldier in connection with your brand.\nNike is a global sports brand with millions of customers around the world, and using imagery associated with a military involved in the ongoing suffering of Palestinian civilians sends a deeply troubling message.\nSports should represent humanity, unity, dignity, and peace — not military occupation or violence against civilians.\nI urge Nike to reconsider this choice and to be mindful of the message your brand communicates through the images and individuals it chooses to represent.\nAs a customer and a member of the global community, I believe companies of Nike’s influence have a responsibility to avoid imagery that can be perceived as endorsing or normalizing violence and oppression.\nI hope you will take this concern seriously and reconsider your use of this image.",
